src/platform: what the game needs from the operating system beyond the standard library
================================================================================================

Four headers in include/platform/ (namespace platform), two implementations chosen by CMake (`xfnv_platform`, a
static library): Win32/ holds the Win32 calls the exe makes, unchanged; Posix/ the POSIX side (Linux: /proc is read
where noted), SDL3 where SDL covers it. No `#if` in either. Everything compiled against the game's headers gets
these headers and the library through `xfnv_game_options`.

Paths.h
-------
NativePath(gamePath)
    Win32: the path as given. POSIX: `\` becomes `/`; the path as given when it exists; else each component is
    looked up case-insensitively (ASCII) in its folder. A component with no match, and every one after it, keeps
    the given case, so a new file keeps the case of its existing folders and its own given case. Of names differing
    only in case, an exact match wins, else the first in byte order. Each folder's listing is cached and read again
    when the folder's device, inode or modification time changes, so creates, deletes and renames by anyone (the
    game's own fopen included) are seen without being reported.
FindFiles(gamePattern)
    FindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA's entries: name, 64-bit size, FILE_ATTRIBUTE_* bits, write, creation and last
    access times as FILETIME values, the 8.3 short name. `*` and `?` in the last component, case-insensitive, `*.*`
    matches every name; a pattern without wildcards gives the one entry with its on-disk spelling. POSIX: `.` and
    `..` first, then by upper-cased name (NTFS's order; Wine gives the same); attributes as Wine reports them
    (directory or archive, read-only without the owner's write bit, hidden for dot files); the creation time is
    statx's birth time where the file system records one, else the write time; the short name is empty. DOS
    short-name matches and `?` matching nothing at a name's end are not modelled.
UserFolder(LocalAppData | Documents)
    SHGetFolderPathA's CSIDL_LOCAL_APPDATA / CSIDL_PERSONAL, without a trailing separator. POSIX (the user's
    decision, XDG only): `$XDG_DATA_HOME` (default `~/.local/share`) and `$XDG_DATA_HOME/FalloutNV/Documents`; the
    game appends `\FalloutNV\` and `\My Games\FalloutNV\` itself. POSIX creates the folder (Windows' exist).
InstallFolder()
    With a trailing separator. Win32: HKLM\Software\Bethesda Softworks\FalloutNV "Installed Path" (empty when
    missing). POSIX: the executable's folder (/proc/self/exe).
UserName()
    GetUserNameA; POSIX: the passwd entry's name, else $USER.

Ini.h (GetPrivateProfile*/WritePrivateProfile*; Win32 calls them, POSIX parses to Wine's profile.c rules)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Lines end at `\n` (or `\r` where no `\n` follows); lines, section names (inside the brackets), keys and values
  are trimmed of spaces, tabs, CR/LF and the 0x1A end mark; `[name]` up to the last `]` is a header.
- Section and key match case-insensitively; only the first section of a name is searched; its first key wins.
- A value loses one pair of enclosing `"` or `'`; a line without `=` has no value (the default is returned).
- IniGetString: the result is copied to at most out.size() - 1 characters; returns the count. The default loses
  trailing spaces (a one-character default is kept) and its quotes; when the file cannot be read (its folder is
  missing) the default is copied as is. Only the result's characters and one NUL are written.
- IniGetKeys (= a null key): the names of the entries with a value, comments (`;`) skipped, each NUL-terminated,
  an extra NUL at the end; a short buffer truncates the last name and returns out.size() - 2, with the list's two
  NULs at the end (Windows' documented form; Wine writes only one there: the one known difference to Wine).
- IniGetInt: the string read with sign and 0x/0o/0b prefixes (lower-case), up to the first non-digit, wrapping in
  32 bits; the default when the key is missing or empty.
- IniWriteString: the value loses its leading spaces; a null value deletes the key, a null key the section; false
  when the file cannot be written (a missing folder). POSIX edits the file in place as Windows does: the key's line
  is replaced, a new key goes after its section's last entry, a new section at the end; every other line is kept;
  the file is written with CRLF. Wine instead rewrites the whole file; reads give the same either way.
- Files are cached per path and read again when their device, inode, size or time changes.

Memory.h
--------
Reserve(size, address = nullptr)
    MEM_RESERVE: no access, no memory. With an address: exactly there (64 KB-aligned) or nullptr. POSIX: an
    anonymous PROT_NONE MAP_NORESERVE mapping, 64 KB-aligned like Windows'; with an address, mmap's hint is checked
    and refused when not honoured.
Commit / Decommit(address, size)
    MEM_COMMIT read-write / MEM_DECOMMIT for the pages covering the range, inside a reservation. Fresh or decommitted
    pages read as zero; committed ones keep their contents. POSIX: mprotect; decommit maps fresh PROT_NONE pages over
    the range (memory returned).
Release(base)
    MEM_RELEASE of a whole reservation by Reserve's address (POSIX keeps each reservation's size).
PageSize(), AllocationGranularity()
    4 KB and 64 KB (POSIX: the system's page size; the granularity is fixed at 64 KB as on Windows).
MemoryStatus()
    GlobalMemoryStatusEx's figures in bytes. POSIX: physical from sysconf and /proc/meminfo's MemAvailable; page
    file = physical + swap (available: MemAvailable + SwapFree); virtual = the 47-bit user space minus the process's
    size. The 32-bit program's GlobalMemoryStatus (not Ex) caps at 4 GB; a site printing a 32-bit field clamps.

System.h
--------
SetThreadPriority(thread, THREAD_PRIORITY_*), SetCurrentThreadIdealProcessor(n)
    Win32: the calls. POSIX: no effect (true): a normal thread's priority cannot be raised without privileges, and
    there is no soft processor hint.
SetThreadName(thread, name), SetCurrentThreadName(name)
    Win32: the debugger's 0x406D1388 exception inside __try, raised only while a debugger is attached (the exe's
    form). POSIX: pthread_setname_np, the first 15 characters, always.
ShowMessageBox(text, caption, MB_* type)
    MessageBoxA with no owner, returning IDOK..IDCONTINUE. POSIX: SDL_ShowMessageBox with the type's buttons in
    Windows' order and labels, MB_DEFBUTTONn as the Return default, Cancel (or a lone OK) as Escape and on close,
    MB_ICONERROR/WARNING else information; without a display the text goes to stderr and the result is 0
    (MessageBoxA's failure). MB_TOPMOST and the other flags have no effect. SDL shows boxes on the main thread only:
    another thread's box goes to the main thread through SDL_RunOnMainThread and is shown at its next event pump,
    or on the calling thread when the main thread has not taken it within half a second (it can be loading, showing
    another box or waiting on that thread).
MessageBoxCancelTextBegin(text) / MessageBoxCancelTextActive() / MessageBoxCancelTextEnd()
    MessageHandler's "Yes to all": the calling thread's next message box shows its Cancel button with the text.
    Win32: the exe's WH_CBT hook on the thread (SetWindowsHookExA), which finds the box's "Cancel" button on
    activation, renames it and unhooks itself. POSIX: ShowMessageBox's Cancel label, taken by the next box the same
    thread shows.
RemoteSession()
    GetSystemMetrics(SM_REMOTESESSION) != 0. POSIX: false.
LauncherAvailable()
    Whether FalloutNVLauncher.exe can be started when the display settings do not fit the adapter. Win32: true
    (the game starts it and exits). POSIX: false; the game then writes FalloutPrefs.ini itself (CreateDisplayDriver,
    src/Fallout Shared/Renderer.cpp) and carries on.
SingleInstance(name)
    False when another process holds the name. Win32: CreateMutexA + ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS (handle kept). POSIX: an
    fcntl write lock on `<LocalAppData>/FalloutNV/<name>.lock`, kept open; true when the file cannot be made.
DebuggerPresent / DebuggerBreak / DebuggerOutput
    IsDebuggerPresent, DebugBreak, OutputDebugStringA. POSIX: TracerPid in /proc/self/status, raise(SIGTRAP) (ends
    the process without a debugger, as DebugBreak's unhandled breakpoint does), the text on stderr.
LibraryLoad / LibrarySymbol / LibraryFree
    LoadLibraryA, GetProcAddress, FreeLibrary. POSIX: dlopen(RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL) / dlsym / dlclose;
    `D3D9.DLL` in any case loads `libdxvk_d3d9.so.0` (dxvk-native); other `.dll` names fail, so the game's
    not-found paths run (ATI ADL, ATIMGPUD, dbghelp).
Open(pathOrUrl)
    ShellExecuteA(nullptr, "open", target, ..., SW_SHOWNORMAL), true above 32. (The exe's two sites pass "open"/
    SW_SHOW and a null verb/SW_SHOWNORMAL; for a new process both show it normally.) POSIX: a URL as given, else
    the absolute NativePath as a percent-encoded file:// URL, to SDL_OpenURL; a `.exe` path fails (false) without
    reaching the desktop, as there is no Windows program to run (the game's launcher).
MouseSettings()
    Win32: SwapMouseButton's state (read and restored), GetDoubleClickTime, HKCU\Control Panel\Mouse
    "MouseSensitivity" through atoi (6 when missing). POSIX: no swap, 500 ms, 10 (Windows' defaults).
RegistryOpen/Close/Read/Write
    RegSettingCollection's store. Win32: HKLM\<key> with KEY_ALL_ACCESS (create or open), RegSetValueExA,
    RegQueryValueExA (false and the needed size when the buffer is short). POSIX: the section [key] of
    `<LocalAppData>/FalloutNV/Registry.ini` through Ini; a value is `name=<type>:<data>`, REG_SZ data as quoted
    text (its size counts the NUL), any other type as hex bytes. Opening without create fails while the section has
    no values.
CommandLine()
    The arguments, the program first. Win32: CommandLineToArgvW(GetCommandLineW()) as UTF-8. POSIX: argv.
QuitOnDisplayLoss(window)
    The window's display connection lost becomes one SDL_EVENT_QUIT, so the game leaves through its quit path.
    Win32: no effect. POSIX: on X11, a process-wide Xlib I/O error handler that reports once and returns, and an
    I/O error exit handler (XSetIOErrorExitHandler, libX11 1.7+) on the window's Display that pushes the event and
    returns; Xlib's defaults of both call exit() (under the game's live threads). Xlib's core calls on the broken
    display then fail; extension requests can crash (libXi's grab calls). SDL's second Display (its wake-up
    requests) keeps the default exit handler: the game only polls, so nothing waits to be woken. Wayland: SDL sends
    the quit itself.
DisplayLost()
    Whether QuitOnDisplayLoss saw the connection go: src/platform/dinput_sdl then leaves the mouse grab alone. Win32:
    false.

Posix/Main.cpp
--------------
`main` keeps argv for CommandLine(), joins the arguments after the program's name into WinMain's lpCmdLine (an
argument with a space or tab, or an empty one, quoted) and returns the game's
`WinMain(nullptr, nullptr, lpCmdLine, SW_SHOWNORMAL)`.

Posix/Runtime.cpp
-----------------
vcruntime's `_CxxThrowException` (rt::_CxxThrowException's target, src/SDK/MSVC/ehdata.cpp), which Windows links
from vcruntime: an MSVC throw record cannot be raised through the Itanium ABI, so it reports the call on stderr and
aborts.
